* Provenance: derived for circsim from manufacturer datasheet operating points by scripts/fit-model-cards.mjs (1N4148, 1N4001, 1N5819, SMAJ24A); other cards written by hand from datasheet figures, MIT.
* These are in-house .model cards derived from published datasheet electrical
* characteristics (Vf @ If, Cj, trr, Vbr, Ir). The numeric datasheet parameters
* (facts, not copyrightable expression) inform the standard ngspice level-1
* diode parameter set.
*
* The 1N4148, 1N4001, 1N5819 and SMAJ24A cards are the output of
* scripts/fit-model-cards.mjs: a two-point Vf fit (is, rs) at a stated emission
* coefficient n, junction capacitance from the stated Cj at its stated bias,
* tt from trr, bv/ibv from the stated breakdown point. Nothing is read from any
* third-party library card, and
* src/core/models/__tests__/library-fingerprint.test.ts fails CI if a bundled
* card's parameter tuple matches a known PSpice or LTspice library card.
*
* Values that are NOT datasheet figures (device-class assumptions): the
* emission coefficient n (1.8 small-signal, 1.9 rectifier, 1.05 Schottky, 1.5
* TVS forward path), junction grading m=0.5 and potential vj=0.7 V (0.5 V
* Schottky) because no C-V curve is sampled, typical Cj taken as 0.75 x the
* stated maximum where only a maximum is given, typical Vf taken as 0.9 x the
* stated maximum where only a maximum is given, tt equal to trr, and the
* 1N4001/1N5819 breakdown set 10 percent above the rated VRRM (the datasheet
* only guarantees blocking up to VRRM). The figures themselves are transcribed
* from the datasheet families and are not yet re-verified against vendor PDFs
* row by row. They are checked against resources/models/characterization.json
* (npm run test:characterization).
*
* Diode parameter glossary (ngspice D model):
*   is  - saturation current      n   - emission coefficient
*   rs  - series resistance        cjo - zero-bias junction cap
*   tt  - transit time             bv  - reverse breakdown voltage
*   ibv - current at bv            vj  - junction potential
*   m   - grading coefficient      eg  - bandgap (eV)
*   nbv - breakdown emission coefficient (breakdown slope)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N4148 / 1N914 small-signal fast switching silicon diode.
* Inputs: Vf 0.67V @ 5mA (window 0.62-0.72V midpoint) and 0.9V @ 100mA (1.0V
* max x 0.9), n=1.8; Cj 4pF max @ 0V (x 0.75); trr 4ns; V(BR) 100V @ 100uA.
.model D1N4148 D(is=3.12n rs=0.953 n=1.8 cjo=3p vj=0.7 m=0.5 bv=100 ibv=100u
+ eg=1.11 xti=3 tt=4n)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N4001 general-purpose silicon rectifier (1A, 50V).
* Inputs: Vf 0.93V typ @ 1A and ~0.62V @ 10mA (typical curve, approximate),
* n=1.9; Cj 15pF typ @ 4V; trr ~2us; VRRM 50V (card breakdown 55V, 10uA).
.model D1N4001 D(is=33.8n rs=84.5m n=1.9 cjo=38.9p vj=0.7 m=0.5 bv=55 ibv=10u
+ eg=1.11 xti=3 tt=2u)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 1N5819 Schottky barrier rectifier (1A, 40V).
* Inputs: Vf 0.54V @ 1A and 0.81V @ 3A (0.6V and 0.9V max x 0.9), n=1.05;
* Cj ~110pF typ @ 4V; VRRM 40V (card breakdown 44V at 1mA, IR 1mA max at
* rated VR); Schottky eg=0.69 and xti=2; no minority storage (tt omitted).
.model D1N5819 D(is=193n rs=0.12 n=1.05 cjo=330p vj=0.5 m=0.5 bv=44 ibv=1m
+ eg=0.69 xti=2)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* SS54 / SB540 Schottky barrier rectifier (5A, 40V, DO-214AB/SMC).
* Datasheet typ: Vf=0.55V @ 5A (is/n set the junction drop, rs=30 mohm adds
* the ohmic part); Vbr=40V; Schottky eg=0.69 and xti=2, n near 1.
.model DSS54 D(is=2u rs=0.03 n=1.1 tt=8n cjo=300p vj=0.4 m=0.38
+ bv=40 ibv=1m eg=0.69 xti=2)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* SMAJ24A unidirectional 24V TVS (SMA, 400W): standoff 24V, breakdown
* 26.7-29.5V @ 1mA, clamping 38.9V @ 10.3A, Cj~280pF. Terminals: a (anode,
* position 1), k (cathode, position 2), the same positions as the model-card
* diodes, so the index.json pinMaps are unchanged.
* Inputs: forward Vf ~1.0V @ 1A and 3.15V @ 25A (3.5V max x 0.9), n=1.5;
* VBR 28.1V @ 1mA (window midpoint); VC 38.9V @ 10.3A.
* Two separate paths, so the forward drop does not inherit the clamp slope:
*   forward:  DF a->k, rs (84 mohm) fitted to the forward points only.
*   reverse:  k -> DB (blocking diode) -> m -> DZ (breakdown diode, rs carries
*             the clamp slope) -> a. DB blocks when the TVS is forward biased.
* bv and rs of DZ solve V(1mA) = VBR and V(10.3A) = VC including DB's drop.
.subckt DSMAJ24A a k
df a k DSMAJ24A_F
db k m DSMAJ24A_B
dz a m DSMAJ24A_Z
.model DSMAJ24A_F D(is=56.3p rs=84.4m n=1.5 cjo=280p vj=0.7 m=0.5 eg=1.11)
.model DSMAJ24A_B D(is=1p rs=10m n=1 bv=100)
.model DSMAJ24A_Z D(is=1p rs=0.992 n=1 bv=27.6 ibv=1m)
.ends DSMAJ24A

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BZX55C5V1 / 5V1 zener diode (Vz=5.1V @ 5mA).
* Reverse breakdown modeled via bv/ibv; forward path is an ordinary Si diode.
.model DZ5V1 D(is=1n rs=0.5 n=1.7 tt=50n cjo=175p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=5.1 ibv=5m eg=1.11)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BZX84C3V0 / 3V0 zener diode (Vz=3.0V @ 1mA - soft low-voltage knee).
* Reverse breakdown modeled via bv/ibv; forward path is an ordinary Si diode.
.model DZ3V0 D(is=1n rs=0.6 n=1.7 tt=50n cjo=450p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=3.0 ibv=1m eg=1.11)
